{
  "title": "Migration explorer — downloadable official extracts",
  "license": "Most files are Crown copyright, reusable under OGL v3.0. Academic citations are cite-only.",
  "ogl": "https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/",
  "howRefreshWorks": {
    "download": "npm run download  (or bash scripts/download-raw.sh). Resume-safe unless FORCE=1 / --force.",
    "build": "npm run build  (normalise geo + ingest). Fails if a critical file is missing or a required sheet/column cannot be parsed.",
    "refresh": "npm run refresh  = download + build + refresh-status stamp. Use npm run refresh:force to re-fetch even when files exist.",
    "schedule": "GitHub Action .github/workflows/refresh.yml runs npm run refresh on a monthly cron and on workflow_dispatch. A failed run is a failed check; it does not invent series. On success the Action commits catalog.json + refresh-status.json + source-health.json + checksum pins if they changed. On failure it commits only the fail stamp and source-health (last-good catalog stays).",
    "partial": "Optional files only warn. Default: any SCHEMA ERROR exits 1 and leaves the previous catalog.json in place. MIG_ALLOW_PARTIAL=1 is a local debug escape — ingest still prints SCHEMA ERROR but writes catalog.json anyway (it may be incomplete).",
    "schemaBreak": "ingest.mjs prints SCHEMA ERROR for a missing critical file, missing sheet, or a series with too few parseable points. Without MIG_ALLOW_PARTIAL=1 the previous public/data/catalog.json is not overwritten.",
    "checksums": "data/checksums.json pins SHA-256 of last ingest-validated extracts. A download whose hash differs is recorded on public/data/source-health.json. Ingest must still parse before catalog.json is replaced — a silent file swap that breaks schema does not go live.",
    "sourceHealth": "public/data/source-health.json lists last OK vs last fail and hash match per feed. The site header shows a red badge when the last refresh failed.",
    "scheduledRefresh": "Prefer `npm run refresh` locally or `.github/workflows/refresh.yml` (monthly cron `17 6 1 * *` plus workflow_dispatch). A failed run is a failed check, writes refresh-status.json + source-health.json, and does not overwrite catalog.json. A Cloudflare Cron Trigger is not shipped."
  },
